note bottom of DUP
  **The UNIQUE column is the whole finding.**
  558 + 559, 745, 1.10 + 1.10 GB: the same
  harness content, written twice, because
  each variant rebuilds it on a second base.
end note

note right of INVERT
  **Proven to build, and it still loses.**
  A spike layered the browser onto
  proveo/opencode: exit 0, Chromium runs at
  uid 4242. It saves 12-20% for one operator
  and costs the fleet 1.17 GB.
end note

note bottom of COST
  **Sharing is the thing being traded.**
  The browser payload is stored once today.
  Inverted it is stored per harness, and it
  is 1.79 GB — larger than every harness
  delta it would deduplicate.
end note

note bottom of CURSOR
  **Three ways out, all with a price.**
  Move cursor onto base-node-lsp (+700 MB on
  the lean image, a second node), install node
  in the layer (re-implements base-node), or
  invert two harnesses and not the third.
end note

note right of C1
  **The Dockerfile already knows.**
  Its ``find '*/chromium-*/*'`` uses a hyphen
  so it will not match the shell — the layer
  installs a browser it then excludes by
  hand, and nothing deletes it.
end note

note right of C2
  **Verified, not assumed.** A jlink runtime
  rendered PlantUML to PNG and SVG at 59 MB.
  Ship the 75 MB module set: jdtls uses the
  floor's java whenever ``_java_major`` says
  21, and would fail on a plantuml-only prune.
end note

note right of C3
  **The fix is already in the repo.**
  egress-proxy copies ``cmd`` and ``internal``
  and nothing else. base copies the whole
  repo — node_modules, .git — into a Go
  builder, and rebuilds it on any edit.
end note

note bottom of DOCKERD
  **Decided by removal, not by evidence.**
  No image ships docker now. If sbx supplies
  no client, `docker: sbx` is a promise four
  manifests cannot keep, and e2e says so in
  those words rather than expecting absence.
end note

note bottom of LABEL
  **The label outlived the pass.**
  Every harness installs root-owned binaries
  after its last proveo-harden, and solidity
  never runs one while inheriting the claim.
end note

note top of FLOOR
  **Cut here and it multiplies.**
  On one host a base-layer saving counts once.
  In the registry it is paid on all 14 images,
  which is why a 119 MB JRE cut outranks a
  2.41 GB dedup that only one host ever sees.
end note

